# OFLIT Child Time Limit — per-user weekly scheduled quotas
#
# Scheduled quotas are optional.
# Users without a section continue using the normal daily quota.
#
# Manage this file with `child-time schedule`; you should not need to
# edit it by hand:
#
#   child-time schedule list   USER
#   child-time schedule add    USER --days DAYS --start HH:MM --end HH:MM --quota DURATION
#   child-time schedule edit   USER SCHEDULE_ID [--days|--start|--end|--quota ...]
#   child-time schedule remove USER SCHEDULE_ID
#
# Format
# ------
#   [DAYS/]HH:MM-HH:MM=SECONDS
#
# DAYS is a weekday expression. When omitted, the schedule applies on
# every weekday and keeps the legacy `HH:MM-HH:MM` identifier, so
# configurations written before weekday support keep working unchanged.
#
#   fri              one weekday
#   mon-fri          an inclusive range
#   sat,sun          a comma-separated list
#   fri-mon          a range that wraps past Sunday (Fri, Sat, Sun, Mon)
#   daily            every weekday (same as omitting DAYS)
#   weekdays         mon-fri
#   weekend          sat,sun
#
# Example — afternoons every day, plus a Friday morning slot:
#
# [azzahra]
# 15:00-17:00=3600
# fri/09:00-12:00=3600
#
# Rules:
# - Same-day slots only; overnight slots are not supported.
# - Slots that apply on the same weekday must not overlap.
# - Slot quota is measured as active-use seconds.
# - Slot quota must not exceed the slot's wall-clock length.
# - Unused quota does not carry over to another slot or another day.
# - For every weekday, the total quota of that day's slots must not
#   exceed that day's effective daily limit (see child-time-daily.conf).
# - Each slot's identifier is its canonical `[DAYS/]HH:MM-HH:MM` string.
#   Changing a slot's days or window changes its identifier, and that
#   slot's usage for today restarts from zero.
